./redteam/reports/stage_195.md:152:The mathematics holds up: I hand-verified the odd ratio (lines 64–67), the Δ_norm collapse and its Δ_Q form (lines 90, 94–97), the point-particle reductions (lines 111–116), the DtN-deformation χ_Q/N_Q/Δ_norm^pt forms (lines 139–143), the first-order linearization (lines 160–163, numerator first-order `15S·eps_beta + dSigma0 + 27dSigma5` over `3S` gives `−5eps_beta − dSigma0/(3S) − 9dSigma5/S`), and all canonical-branch specializations (lines 174–183) — these are genuine, non-tautological, and match the notes. Symbol domains are physically sound (no `symbol_assumption_error`); denominators `3S−Σ₀` and `Sβ⁵+9Σ₅` stay generically nonzero. The defect is that the stage's named headline — the boxed `\stagefield{Output}` `m̂₀²χ_Q N_Q=1` — is verified only by a self-comparison (`odd_closure − odd_closure`, line 89) instead of being derived from the observable odd condition `m̂₀²Γ̄₅=Γ̄₅^target` plus the verified ratio (F1, medium), with two further low-severity definitional echoes (F2). The fix is a small, mechanical SymPy edit that composes existing in-script quantities, introducing no new constant and no paper drift. Hence `verdict: findings`, `paper_alignment: partial`, no stop_cold.
