./redteam/verifications/stage_105.md:70:The 9 PASS lines (sigma_Q normalization; omega^2 / omega^4 real coeffs; imag omega^5 coeff; chi_Q-1; deformed const / z^2 / z^4 / imag-z^5) each correspond to a real, content-bearing assertion — none is X-X. The chi_Q-1 PASS (the central paper claim) is solved via Reduce, not asserted. No `ReplaceAll`/argt/symbol-assumption warnings anywhere in the log.
./redteam/verifications/stage_105.md:78:No derived result changed. The `.py` (source of any downstream-consumed values) was untouched except for the F2 label strings. The `.wl` was rewritten to a different algebraic route but reproduces identical results (chi_Q=1, same coefficient values), serving as an independent cross-check rather than altering a downstream quantity. Downstream units (Stages 106+) read chi_Q=1 and the deformed-branch coefficients; neither moved, so no downstream re-audit is warranted on math grounds. (The orchestrator's blanket `upstream_stale: true` for units > 105 is routine bookkeeping, not a substantive concern.)
