./redteam/codex_reviews/stage_169.md.raw:731:/var/projects/toy_physics/research/pde_ledger/redteam/codex_reviews/stage_112.md.raw:798:/var/projects/toy_physics/research/pde_ledger/notes/MATHEMATICA_MIRROR_POLICY.md:18:IV.2 audit (2026-05-27) caught `mathematica_transliteration` patterns on 5 of 7 dirty stages (105 — full `.wl` rewrite with structurally distinct path: unfactored ratio + `Apart` round-trip check + `SeriesCoefficient` operator form + `Reduce`-over-reals for chi_Q + polynomial inversion of `Λ·Y = -3` for the deformed branch; variable names changed (no `yRet`/`lamDef`/`yDef`/`omegaQ`/`sigmaCan`). 106 — full `.wl` re-author starting from the retarded one-pole form `Y_ret(omega) = 3/4 + (1/4)/(1 - omega^2/OmegaQ^2 - i chi_Q sigma_Q^can omega^5)`, series-expanding to omega^7 to show next odd term is at O(omega^7), with no `nqGeneral`/`k0`/`k2`/`k4`/`gamma5` intermediates; closure to N_Q=1 via source-map relation. 109 — linearization rewrite via numerator/denominator-separate series + `Series[1/denominator]` inversion + multiply, solving `chiSeries - 1 == 0` directly for `a5` without the `coeff = (chiSeries - 1)/eps` intermediate. 111 — added independent chi_Q^mix re-derivation block bypassing the L0/L5 extraction (geometric-series form of the pole alone), plus new `expectZero["chi_Q^mix routes agree", chiMix - chiMixAlt]`. 112 — added independent Stage-92 linearized cross-check extracting `(a_0, a_5) = (3 sigma, -sigma gamma)` from solB's deformation and solving the preservation condition `a_0/3 + 9 a_5 = 0` for `gamma_W = 1/9`, an algebraically distinct route from the chi_Q-based solve). Transliteration share for IV.2 = 5/7 = 71% dirty; higher than IV.1 (4/11 = 36%) but several of these were borderline mathematical mirrors where the structural rewrite added genuine engine independence rather than pure renaming. **No new pitfall candidates** from IV.2 — all orchestrator-direct edits applied first-attempt clean. But pitfall #11 (PASS-line discipline) was **re-confirmed prominently**: 108 F2 caught `chiArg /. beta -> 1 - 1` parsing as `(chiArg /. (beta -> 0))` because Mathematica `Plus`/`Subtract` binds tighter than `Rule`. The buggy assertion `0^5 = 0` had been silently passing on every prior run; only the auditor's structural read caught it. Fix: `(chiArg /. beta -> 1) - 1`. This is a **persistent class of silent-pass bug** — any directive instructing Codex to write `expr /. var -> value <op> rest` must use explicit parentheses around the `Rule`, or the parser bends the bracket. Augment pitfall #11 with: Mathematica `/.` (ReplaceAll) binds looser than `+`/`-`/`*`/`/`/`^` but Rule binds even looser; always parenthesize `(expr /. rule)` when followed by arithmetic.
