./redteam/pass2/codex_logs/184_iter1.txt:738:paper/appendices/stage_appendix_part05.tex:265:Stages 164--168 translate the first off-family normal coordinate into explicit microscopic transport variables and then separate on-bundle tangent motion from off-bundle slippage.  Stages 169--173 prove that grouped real \(P_2\) anisotropy does not linearly feed scalar slippage, derive the direct outlet map, and collapse the even-preserving grouped defect to \(\Xi_{\rm load}\).  Stages 174--180 factor \(\Xi_{\rm load}\) through wall-referenced self-similarity, outgoing-load factors, port co-loading, and the effective transfer shape, giving \(\Xi_1=P_1/P_0\).  Stages 181--185 pass from physical coherent-kernel variables to the triangular normal form and then to direct microscopic monomials.  Stages 186--187 prove the finite orbit--fibre theorem.  Stages 188--192 build the observable, transfer-shape, finite-packet, and projector compilers.  Stages 193--197 close the branch-side Packet-A finish line to \(\Delta_Q=\chi_Q-1\).  Stages 198--200 remove the orbit representative and combine Packet A and Packet B into \eqref{eq:app-part05-theorem-finalpacket}.
