     1	# Moving-Throat PDE — Stage 182: Microscopic Coherent-Kernel Slippage Decomposition and the Exact Tracking/Nontracking Split
     2	
     3	## Purpose
     4	
     5	Stage 181 reduced the weak-axisymmetric grouped defect on the actual coherent local D/N tracking branch to the physical placement variables
     6	\[
     7	\Xi_1
     8	=
     9	\zeta_Z-\omega_W+\frac{2\chi_1}{1+\chi_0}
    10	+\frac{2\epsilon_1}{1-\epsilon},
    11	\qquad
    12	\epsilon
    13	=
    14	\epsilon_W\!\left[1-\frac{2}{11}\frac{\delta_U}{1+\delta_U}\right],
    15	\]
    16	with
    17	\[
    18	\epsilon_1
    19	=
    20	\left(1-\frac{2}{11}\frac{\delta_U}{1+\delta_U}\right)\varepsilon_W
    21	-
    22	\frac{2\epsilon_W}{11(1+\delta_U)^2}\,\delta_{U,1}.
    23	\]
    24	It also showed that the coherent support ratio \(\zeta\) drops out identically, and that exact tracking-factor rigidity is not enough to kill \(\Xi_1\).
    25	
    26	So the next honest step is now very small:
    27	
    28	> push the Stage 181 physical variables one layer deeper, down to the actual microscopic coherent-kernel couplings, and identify which microscopic slippages really carry the grouped defect.
    29	
    30	That is what this stage does.
    31	
    32	The main result is that the coherent weak-axisymmetric defect depends on only four microscopic slippage combinations:
    33	\[
    34	\Sigma_Z,
    35	\qquad
    36	\Sigma_\chi,
    37	\qquad
    38	\Sigma_\epsilon,
    39	\qquad
    40	\Sigma_\delta,
    41	\]
    42	while the selected-branch form introduces one additional dressing slippage \(\Sigma_\eta\).
    43	Explicitly,
    44	\[
    45	\boxed{
    46	\Xi_1
    47	=
    48	\Sigma_Z
    49	+\frac{2\chi_0}{1+\chi_0}\,\Sigma_\chi
    50	+\frac{2\epsilon_W}{1-\epsilon}
    51	\left[
    52	\frac{11+9\delta_U}{11(1+\delta_U)}\,\Sigma_\epsilon
    53	-\frac{2\delta_U}{11(1+\delta_U)^2}\,\Sigma_\delta
    54	\right].
    55	}
    56	\]
    57	Moreover, the tracking-factor drift depends on only one particular combination
    58	\[
    59	\boxed{
    60	\Sigma_{\rm tr}:=(1+\chi_0)\Sigma_\delta+(1+\delta_U)\Sigma_\chi,
    61	}
    62	\]
    63	through
    64	\[
    65	\boxed{
    66	\Theta_1
    67	=
    68	-\frac{\chi_0\delta_U}{(1+\chi_0)(1+\delta_U)(1+\chi_0+\delta_U)}\,\Sigma_{\rm tr}.
    69	}
    70	\]
    71	So the grouped defect splits exactly into a tracking piece and a genuinely nontracking mixed/outgoing piece.
    72	
    73	The strongest sharpened conclusion is therefore:
    74	
    75	- coherent support remains absent,
    76	- exact tracking rigidity means \(\Sigma_{\rm tr}=0\),
    77	- but the grouped defect still survives unless the nontracking microscopic slippages also vanish.
    78	
    79	---
    80	
    81	## 1. Microscopic coherent-kernel variables
    82	
    83	Stage 047 already expressed the coherent local D/N branch in terms of the microscopic couplings
    84	\[
    85	\epsilon_\eta=\frac{c_{\eta U}^2}{K_U K_\eta^{(\mathrm{eff})}},
    86	\qquad
    87	\chi_0=\frac{\gamma c_{\eta U}}{K_U},
    88	\qquad
    89	\epsilon_W=\frac{\gamma^2\lambda_W^2\sigma}{K_U K_W^{(\mathrm{eff})}},
    90	\]
    91	\[
    92	Z_W=\frac{\lambda_W^2}{K_\eta^{(\mathrm{eff})}K_W^{(\mathrm{eff})}},
    93	\qquad
    94	\delta_U=\frac{\pi^2 T_U}{L^2 K_U},
    95	\qquad
    96	\Omega_W^2=\frac{K_W^{(\mathrm{eff})}}{\mu_W}.
    97	\]
    98	The support lane enters through
    99	\[
   100	\zeta=\frac{\lambda_\phi^2 K_W^{(\mathrm{eff})}}{\lambda_W^2 K_\phi^{(\mathrm{eff})}},
   101	\]
   102	but Stage 181 already showed that \(\zeta\) drops out of the grouped defect.
   103	
   104	So the natural microscopic weak-axisymmetric logarithmic drifts are
   105	\[
   106	\delta\ln \lambda_{W,A}=\epsilon\lambda_A\,\lambda_1,
   107	\qquad
   108	\delta\ln c_{\eta U,A}=\epsilon\lambda_A\,c_1,
   109	\qquad
   110	\delta\ln \gamma_A=\epsilon\lambda_A\,\gamma_1,
   111	\]
   112	\[
   113	\delta\ln K_{U,A}=\epsilon\lambda_A\,\kappa_U,
   114	\qquad
   115	\delta\ln K_{\eta,A}^{(\mathrm{eff})}=\epsilon\lambda_A\,\kappa_\eta,
   116	\qquad
   117	\delta\ln K_{W,A}^{(\mathrm{eff})}=\epsilon\lambda_A\,\kappa_W,
   118	\]
   119	\[
   120	\delta\ln \mu_{W,A}=\epsilon\lambda_A\,\mu_1,
   121	\qquad
   122	\delta\ln T_{U,A}=\epsilon\lambda_A\,\tau_1.
   123	\]
   124	Because the grouped weak-axisymmetric branch keeps the scalar size variables lane-invariant at first order, the axial scale \(L\) is held fixed here. If one later wants an explicit effective axial-size drift, it can be restored by replacing
   125	\[
   126	\Sigma_\delta=\tau_1-\kappa_U
   127	\]
   128	with
   129	\[
   130	\Sigma_\delta=\tau_1-\kappa_U-2\ell_{L,1}.
   131	\]
   132	At the present level we keep \(\ell_{L,1}=0\).
   133	
   134	---
   135	
   136	## 2. Exact physical-branch drifts from the microscopic variables
   137	
   138	Differentiating the Stage-047 coherent ratios gives the physical Stage 181 drift variables directly.
   139	
   140	### 2.1 Direct port variables
   141	
   142	For the wall-to-mixed overlap ratio,
   143	\[
   144	Z_W=\frac{\lambda_W^2}{K_\eta^{(\mathrm{eff})}K_W^{(\mathrm{eff})}},
   145	\]
   146	we get
   147	\[
   148	\boxed{
   149	\zeta_Z=2\lambda_1-\kappa_\eta-\kappa_W.
   150	}
   151	\]
   152	
   153	For the mixed frequency scale,
   154	\[
   155	\Omega_W^2=\frac{K_W^{(\mathrm{eff})}}{\mu_W},
   156	\]
   157	we get
   158	\[
   159	\boxed{
   160	\omega_W=\kappa_W-\mu_1.
   161	}
   162	\]
   163	
   164	For the interference ratio,
   165	\[
   166	\chi_0=\frac{\gamma c_{\eta U}}{K_U},
   167	\]
   168	we get
   169	\[
   170	\boxed{
   171	\chi_1=\chi_0\,(\gamma_1+c_1-\kappa_U).
   172	}
   173	\]
   174	
   175	For the wall/internal dressing ratio,
   176	\[
   177	\epsilon_\eta=\frac{c_{\eta U}^2}{K_U K_\eta^{(\mathrm{eff})}},
   178	\]
   179	we get
   180	\[
   181	\boxed{
   182	\eta_1=\epsilon_\eta\,(2c_1-\kappa_U-\kappa_\eta).
   183	}
   184	\]
   185	
   186	For the unsplit mixed blocking ratio,
   187	\[
   188	\epsilon_W=\frac{\gamma^2\lambda_W^2\sigma}{K_U K_W^{(\mathrm{eff})}},
   189	\]
   190	we get
   191	\[
   192	\boxed{
   193	\varepsilon_W=\epsilon_W\,(2\gamma_1+2\lambda_1-\kappa_U-\kappa_W).
   194	}
   195	\]
   196	
   197	For the split-\(U\) axial ratio,
   198	\[
   199	\delta_U=\frac{\pi^2 T_U}{L^2 K_U},
   200	\]
   201	we get
   202	\[
   203	\boxed{
   204	\delta_{U,1}=\delta_U\,(\tau_1-\kappa_U).
   205	}
   206	\]
   207	
   208	### 2.2 Support variables are absent
   209	
   210	The microscopic support quantities
   211	\[
   212	\lambda_\phi,
   213	\qquad
   214	K_\phi^{(\mathrm{eff})}
   215	\]
   216	enter the coherent branch only through \(\zeta\), and Stage 181 already proved that \(\zeta\) drops out of
   217	\[
   218	\mathcal T^2,
   219	\qquad
   220	R_{\mathrm{target}},

