 succeeded in 0ms:
     1	# Moving-Throat PDE — Stage 047: Exact Coherent-Kernel Dimensionless Map and the Support-Enhancement Factor
     2	
     3	## Purpose
     4	
     5	Stage 046 left the reduced theorem gap in its sharpest form so far:
     6	
     7	> the first coherent local D/N kernel lands on the physical tracking branch, but the constructive split-`U` deformation lowers `R_tr` below `1` and therefore worsens the normalization target relative to the old flat branch.
     8	
     9	That was already useful, but the actual kernel-strength question was still spread over too many dimensional couplings.
    10	
    11	The next honest move is therefore to compress the coherent local kernel to the smallest exact **dimensionless placement map** and identify how the support lane enters the branch.
    12	
    13	This stage does that.
    14	
    15	The main result is that, on the coherent tracking branch identified in Stage 045, the first coherent local D/N kernel collapses to a very small parameter set:
    16	
    17	- one wall/internal dressing ratio `eps_eta`,
    18	- one split-`U` axial ratio `delta_U`,
    19	- one common interference ratio `chi_0`,
    20	- one mixed blocking ratio `eps_W`,
    21	- one wall-to-mixed overlap ratio `Z_W`,
    22	- one support-to-mixed amplitude ratio `zeta`,
    23	- and one radiative demand scale `Lambda`.
    24	
    25	In those variables the coherent branch is fully described by
    26	
    27	`R_tr = [ 1 + chi_0/(1+delta_U) ] / (1 + chi_0),`
    28	
    29	`eps = eps_W^(split) = eps_W [ 1 - (2/11) delta_U/(1+delta_U) ],`
    30	
    31	`delta = [ delta_0 + eps_eta delta_U/(1+delta_U) ] / (1 - eps_eta),`
    32	
    33	`M_mix = 8 Z_W (1 + chi_0)^2 / [ pi^2 (1 - eps_eta) (1 - eps) ],`
    34	
    35	`M_supp = 8 zeta Z_W (1 + chi_0)^2 / [ pi^2 (1 - eps_eta) (1 - zeta eps) ],`
    36	
    37	`R_target = Lambda (1 - eps_eta) (1 - eps)^2 / [ Z_W (1 + chi_0)^2 ].`
    38	
    39	So the entire support lane enters through one exact factor
    40	
    41	`S(zeta;eps) := M_tr / M_mix = 1 + zeta(1-eps)/(1-zeta eps),`
    42	
    43	with
    44	
    45	`M_tr = M_mix S(zeta;eps).`
    46	
    47	That turns the support problem into a one-parameter enhancement problem rather than a diffuse multidimensional closure question.
    48	
    49	---
    50	
    51	## 1. Coherent local interaction data
    52	
    53	On the coherent local D/N branch from Stage 045 the mixed and support lanes couple through the same local source density,
    54	
    55	`L_int^(coh)`
    56	`= - int_0^L ds [ lambda_W W + lambda_phi phi ] [ eta - gamma U ].`
    57	
    58	So the continuum couplings obey
    59	
    60	`c_(etaW) = lambda_W,`
    61	
    62	`c_(UW)   = gamma lambda_W,`
    63	
    64	`c_(etaphi) = lambda_phi,`
    65	
    66	`c_(Uphi)   = gamma lambda_phi.`
    67	
    68	The wall/internal coupling `c_(etaU)` remains independent.
    69	
    70	The split-`U` stiffness is
    71	
    72	`K_(U1) = K_U (1 + delta_U),`
    73	
    74	with
    75	
    76	`delta_U = pi^2 T_U / (L^2 K_U).`
    77	
    78	The effective wall and D/N support stiffnesses are
    79	
    80	`K_eta^(eff) = K_eta + 6 T_Omega,`
    81	
    82	`K_W^(eff)   = K_W   + pi^2 T_W   / (4 L^2),`
    83	
    84	`K_phi^(eff) = K_phi + pi^2 T_phi / (4 L^2).`
    85	
    86	As before,
    87	
    88	`sigma = kappa_0^2 + kappa_1^2 = 88 / (9 pi^2).`
    89	
    90	---
    91	
    92	## 2. Exact coherent dimensionless ratios
    93	
    94	The natural coherent-kernel dimensionless ratios are
    95	
    96	`eps_eta := c_(etaU)^2 / ( K_U K_eta^(eff) ),`
    97	
    98	`eps_W   := gamma^2 lambda_W^2 sigma / ( K_U K_W^(eff) ),`
    99	
   100	`Z_W     := lambda_W^2 / ( K_eta^(eff) K_W^(eff) ),`
   101	
   102	`delta_0 := pi^2 T_w / ( L^2 K_eta^(eff) ),`
   103	
   104	`chi_0   := gamma c_(etaU) / K_U,`
   105	
   106	`zeta    := lambda_phi^2 K_W^(eff) / ( lambda_W^2 K_phi^(eff) ),`
   107	
   108	`Lambda  := 27 pi^2 G c_s^5 K_W^(eff) / (20 a^5 c^5 mu_W).`
   109	
   110	Two exact coherent identities then follow immediately:
   111	
   112	`rho_0 = sigma_0 = chi_0,`
   113	
   114	`eps_phi = zeta eps_W,`
   115	
   116	`Z_phi   = zeta Z_W.`
   117	
   118	So the support lane is not independent of the mixed lane at the level of dimensionless couplings. It differs only by the one ratio `zeta`.
   119	
   120	---
   121	
   122	## 3. Exact split data on the coherent branch
   123	
   124	The coherent tracking factor is
   125	
   126	`R_tr = [ 1 + chi_0/(1+delta_U) ] / (1 + chi_0),`
   127	
   128	with the same exact range as Stage 045:
   129	
   130	`1/(1+delta_U) < R_tr < 1`
   131	
   132	on the constructive branch `chi_0 > 0`, `delta_U > 0`.
   133	
   134	The split mixed and support blocking ratios are
   135	
   136	`eps = eps_W^(split)`
   137	`    = eps_W [ 1 - (2/11) delta_U/(1+delta_U) ],`
   138	
   139	`eps_phi^(split) = zeta eps.`
   140	
   141	The geometry anisotropy is still
   142	
   143	`delta = [ delta_0 + eps_eta delta_U/(1+delta_U) ] / (1 - eps_eta).`
   144	
   145	So once the coherent kernel is imposed, the branch direction, the blocking, and the anisotropy are all explicit functions of the same small dimensionless set.
   146	
   147	---
   148	
   149	## 4. Exact mixed/support baselines and support-enhancement factor
   150	
   151	The mixed baseline becomes
   152	
   153	`M_mix = 8 Z_W (1 + chi_0)^2 / [ pi^2 (1 - eps_eta) (1 - eps) ].`
   154	
   155	Using `Z_phi = zeta Z_W` and `eps_phi^(split) = zeta eps`, the support baseline is
   156	
   157	`M_supp = 8 zeta Z_W (1 + chi_0)^2 / [ pi^2 (1 - eps_eta) (1 - zeta eps) ].`
   158	
   159	Therefore the exact total baseline is
   160	
   161	`M_tr = M_mix + M_supp`
   162	`     = M_mix S(zeta;eps),`
   163	
   164	with the exact support-enhancement factor
   165	
   166	`S(zeta;eps)`
   167	`:= 1 + zeta(1-eps)/(1-zeta eps).`
   168	
   169	This is the cleanest structural simplification of the stage.
   170	

