     1	# Moving-Throat PDE — Stage 105: Exact Fixing of `chi_Q`
     2	
     3	## Goal
     4	
     5	Use the explicit DtN fingerprint to determine the last reduced 2.5PN scalar
     6	\[
     7	\chi_Q
     8	\]
     9	in the canonical retarded grouped-`P2` one-pole-plus-contact module.
    10	
    11	## Retarded minimal isotropic grouped-`P2` module
    12	
    13	Write the retarded normalized quadrupole module as
    14	\[
    15	\widehat Y_Q^{\rm ret}(\omega)
    16	=
    17	\frac34
    18	+
    19	\frac14\,
    20	\frac{1}{
    21	1-\omega^2/\Omega_Q^2
    22	-i\,\chi_Q\,\sigma_Q^{\rm can}\,\omega^5
    23	}
    24	+O(\omega^6).
    25	\]
    26	
    27	The conservative moment match already fixed
    28	\[
    29	\Omega_Q=\frac{3c_s}{2a}.
    30	\]
    31	
    32	Define
    33	\[
    34	\sigma_Q^{\rm can}:=\frac{9}{8\Omega_Q^5}.
    35	\]
    36	Using \(\Omega_Q=3c_s/(2a)\),
    37	\[
    38	\boxed{
    39	\sigma_Q^{\rm can}
    40	=
    41	\frac{4a^5}{27c_s^5}.
    42	}
    43	\]
    44	
    45	## Low-frequency expansion
    46	
    47	Expanding through \(O(\omega^5)\) gives
    48	\[
    49	\widehat Y_Q^{\rm ret}(\omega)
    50	=
    51	1+\frac{a^2\omega^2}{9c_s^2}
    52	+\frac{4a^4\omega^4}{81c_s^4}
    53	+i\,\chi_Q\,\frac{a^5\omega^5}{27c_s^5}
    54	+O(\omega^6).
    55	\]
    56	
    57	From Stage 87, the explicit outgoing DtN branch gives
    58	\[
    59	\widehat Y_2^{\rm out}(\omega)
    60	=
    61	1+\frac{a^2\omega^2}{9c_s^2}
    62	+\frac{4a^4\omega^4}{81c_s^4}
    63	+i\,\frac{a^5\omega^5}{27c_s^5}
    64	+O(\omega^6).
    65	\]
    66	
    67	Matching the \(O(\omega^5)\) coefficient yields
    68	\[
    69	\boxed{\chi_Q=1.}
    70	\]
    71	
    72	So on the canonical compact passive/outgoing grouped-`P2` DtN branch, the last reduced normalization scalar is fixed exactly.
    73	
    74	## General deformed DtN obstruction
    75	
    76	A useful way to parametrize the only remaining PDE-facing freedom is to deform the outgoing DtN operator by
    77	\[
    78	\Lambda_2^{\rm def}(z)
    79	=
    80	-3+\frac{z^2}{3}+\frac{z^4}{9}
    81	+i\,\xi_Q\,\frac{z^5}{9}+O(z^6).
    82	\]
    83	
    84	Then
    85	\[
    86	\widehat Y_2^{\rm def}(z)
    87	=
    88	1+\frac{z^2}{9}
    89	+\frac{4z^4}{81}
    90	+i\,\xi_Q\,\frac{z^5}{27}
    91	+O(z^6),
    92	\]
    93	so
    94	\[
    95	\boxed{\chi_Q=\xi_Q.}
    96	\]
    97	
    98	That means the only reduced 2.5PN obstruction left after the present calculation is a deviation of the actual moving-throat DtN branch from the canonical outgoing `l=2` coefficient \(\xi_Q=1\).

